{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מכשפה", :translit "m'chashefah", :gloss "sorceress"} {:he "המכשף", :translit "ha-m'chashef", :gloss "the sorcerer"} {:he "א' האיש וא' האשה", :translit "alef ha-ish v'alef ha-ishah", :gloss "one alef for the man and one alef for the woman"} {:he "כל שוכב עם בהמה", :translit "kol shochav im b'heimah", :gloss "all who lie with a beast"} {:he "עם", :translit "im", :gloss "with"} {:he "בלעם", :translit "bil'am", :gloss "Balaam"} {:he "זובח לאלהים יחרם", :translit "zoveiach l'elohim yacharam", :gloss "he who slaughters to gods shall be banned"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Letters of המכשף rearrange to מכשפה; the two alefs cover both male and female practitioners"} {:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "כל שוכב עם", :spells "בלעם"}], :frame {:text "Balaam is identified as a practitioner of sorcery in the verse describing his death (Joshua 13:22), where he is called בלעם בן בעור הקוסם. Balaam's she-ass speaks in Numbers 22:28–30, a narrative the Rabbis read as exposing his degraded practices. The Rabbinic tradition that forbidden sexual relations and idolatrous slaughter are gateways to sorcery is discussed in Sanhedrin 67a–67b.", :sources ["Joshua 13:22" "Numbers 22:28–30" "Sanhedrin 67a" "Sanhedrin 67b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לא תחיה", :translit "lo t'chayeh", :gloss "you shall not let live"} {:he "לא תחיה כל נשמה", :translit "lo t'chayeh kol n'shamah", :gloss "you shall not let live any soul"} {:he "החכמה תחיה בעליה", :translit "ha-chochmah t'chayeh b'alehah", :gloss "wisdom gives life to its possessor"} {:he "והמתה מאיש עד אשה מעולל ועד יונק משור ועד שה", :translit "v'himitem me'ish ad ishah m'olel v'ad yonek mi'shor v'ad seh", :gloss "and you shall strike down from man to woman, from infant to nursing child, from ox to sheep"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["לא תחיה" "לא תחיה כל נשמה" "החכמה תחיה בעליה"]}], :frame {:text "The Amalekites' use of sorcery to evade destruction is addressed in Midra